# Supply-chain hardening (see purocoach-incident-2026-08-06.md):
#
# 1) ignore-scripts: no package lifecycle hooks run on install — the exact
#    vector the 2026-08-06 wiper used. Vite/esbuild/rollup work fine without
#    scripts (platform binaries come via optionalDependencies).
# 2) before: EVERY package (transitive deps included) resolves to the newest
#    version published BEFORE this date — a registry time-machine predating
#    the incident. Direct deps are exact-pinned in package.json as well.
#
# Do NOT install on the compromised host until it has been rebuilt.
# After the first clean install, commit package-lock.json and switch to:
#   npm ci --ignore-scripts
ignore-scripts=true
before=2026-08-01
